{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqf9plgeajc","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"APPROVE both #9 + #10 — two-tier feature-merge prose coherent vs live #8","summary":"Coherence review (hold-merge mode, no merge performed). #9 (self-learn-judge SKILL two-tier APPROVE policy) and #10 (CLAUDE.md + parallel-orchestrate two-tier dispatcher convention) describe the SAME model with no contradiction: Tier-1 = single-attempt judge AUTO-merges approved attempt->FEATURE via merge_attempt(repo_path=<feature worktree>) (cheap/reversible); flat attempt->main stays pure HOLD (MERGE PENDING). Tier-2 = dispatcher-only GATED merge_feature feature->main, NEVER automatic, NEVER the judge's call — stated in BOTH. Matches live #8 primitives exactly: create_feature/overlay.features[key]={feature_branch,feature_worktree,base}, branch_task base=orch/feature/<slug>, merge_attempt(repo_path=<feature wt>) lands on feature, merge_feature gated. Completeness covered: dispatcher stays-on-main (one cwd can't be in N worktrees; EnterWorktree optional single-feature convenience), dispatcher-decides/complexity-axis scope, triviality carve-out (skip feature tier for single-task work), stable-base rationale (main drifts under concurrent agents -> fork off stable feature branch -> main sees one atomic reviewed merge). Changes are surgical/additive; #9's new '### Two-tier APPROVE: feature auto-merge vs main hold' heading slugs to two-tier-approve-feature-auto-merge-vs-main-hold, matching all 3 inbound links; conflict handling mirrors existing step-4 + 'never force a merge' guardrail. {code_review:{notes:'both branches mutually consistent and faithful to live #8; additive, anchors resolve',concerns:[]}, merged:false, awaiting_merge:true, date:'2026-06-15'}","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T13:47:34.238Z","vec":[-0.08471290022134781,-0.00285066245123744,0.011845819652080536,-0.000021837942767888308,0.016114311292767525,-0.031254880130290985,-0.04103538766503334,0.03281094133853912